# 374790906: Wasm type nullability confusion due to non-nullable exnref in catch(_all)_ref ## ClusterFuzz Report ``` Another round of subtle nullability issues in opaque types exploitable through Turboshaft. The commit that introduces this issue is less than seven days old, but I've decided not to hold on to it for a week as it seems that **the exception handling spec itself might have a soundness issue** that could also affect any other engines that depend on it as ground truth. ----- ### VULNE...
The vulnerability is an exnref nullability confusion; the supplied PoC already builds add/read/write primitives, so I’m extracting its core and adapting it for native memory and `catflag`.
